# Subject line: aim for ~50 characters
#         1         2         3         4         5
#12345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890
#                                                 ^ 50
<type>(<scope>): <short summary>

# Body lines: maximum 72 characters
#         1         2         3         4         5         6         7
#123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012
#                                                                       ^ 72
#
# Explain:
# - what changed
# - why the change was needed
# - important design or analytical decisions
# - effects on reproducibility, Python, Power BI, or documentation
#
# Do not repeat the subject line.
#
# Example:
#
# feat(config): add analysis configuration
#
# Add settings.yaml for dataset, study periods, paths, seasonal
# definitions, quality checks, and analysis thresholds.
#
# Keep project configuration outside Python source code so that
# analytical settings can be changed without modifying application
# logic.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# TYPES
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# feat      Add a new feature or analytical capability
# fix       Correct a bug, data issue, or incorrect analysis
# data      Add or change data acquisition or processing
# analysis  Add or change analytical methods or metrics
# viz       Add or change Python or Power BI visualizations
# docs      Documentation only
# test      Add or change tests or validation checks
# refactor  Restructure code without changing expected behaviour
# config    Configuration or dependency changes
# build     Build, packaging, or environment changes
# ci        Continuous integration / GitHub Actions changes
# chore     Maintenance that does not fit another category
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# PROJECT SCOPES
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# api             Calgary Open Data / Socrata retrieval
# config          settings.yaml and project configuration
# classification  Residential and rezoning classification rules
# cleaning        Data cleaning and normalization
# validation      Schema and data-quality validation
# periods         Before/during/post-repeal period logic
# seasons         Seasonal classification
# processing      Processing-time calculations
# community       Community-level analysis
# permits         Development permit analysis
# pipeline        End-to-end processing pipeline
# repository      Repository/data-access layer
# adapter         Calgary dataset adapter
# analysis        General analytical framework
# export          CSV/table/chart exports
# powerbi         Power BI model, measures, or dashboard
# charts          Python visualizations
# tests           Automated tests
# docs            General documentation
# methodology     Methodology documentation
# bias            Bias and mitigation documentation
# references      Sources and related work
# summary         DATA 110 project summary
# presentation    Presentation materials
# readme          README.md
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL FOOTERS
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Breaking change:
# BREAKING CHANGE: <describe incompatible change>
#
# Issue/reference:
# Refs: #123
# Closes: #123
#
# Data snapshot:
# Data-Snapshot: YYYY-MM-DD
#
# Classification version:
# Classification-Version: v1.0
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# GOOD EXAMPLES
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# feat(api): add Calgary permit downloader
#
# Add Socrata repository support for development permit dataset
# 6933-unw5 and save a timestamped raw snapshot for reproducible
# analysis.
#
#
# feat(classification): add permit rule framework
#
# Load classification rules from CSV and apply rules by priority.
# Preserve the matching RuleID so classifications remain auditable.
#
#
# analysis(seasons): add seasonal permit metrics
#
# Classify applications into Fall, Winter, Spring, and Summer and
# distinguish complete seasons from periods truncated by study
# boundaries.
#
#
# fix(periods): correct repeal boundary date
#
# Treat August 3, 2026 as the final day of the During period and
# August 4, 2026 as the beginning of Early Post-Repeal.
#
#
# docs(methodology): document classification process
#
# Explain how observed Calgary permit values are reviewed before
# residential and rezoning-relevant rules are finalized.
#
#
# test(processing): test negative processing days
#
# Add validation cases for missing decision dates and decisions that
# precede application dates.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# COMMIT CHECKLIST
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# [ ] Subject uses imperative wording
# [ ] Subject is approximately 50 characters or fewer
# [ ] Subject does not end with a period
# [ ] Body explains why, not only what
# [ ] Body lines are 72 characters or fewer
# [ ] Tests updated if behaviour changed
# [ ] Documentation updated if methodology changed
# [ ] Generated/raw data has not been committed accidentally
# [ ] No credentials, API tokens, or private information included
#
# Lines beginning with # are ignored by Git.
